      "pageDescription": "Geomob is an event series and podcast for location based service creators and enthusiasts.",
      "evidenceText": "Geomob - geoinnovation for fun or profit Skip to main content Geomob is an event series and podcast for geospatial enthusiasts. We meet every few months in various European cities and provide a relaxed forum to discuss geoinnovation in all forms, whether for fun or profit. Learn more about Geomob Upcoming events Nov 18th, 2026 #geomobLX Nov 25th, 2026 #geomobBER Jan 28th, 2027 #geomobLON Feb 24th, 2027 #geomobBRS March 3rd, 2027 #geomobBER past events Latest podcast episodes 364. Katie Dawson: FRIDAS 16 Nov 2026 Katie Dawson from EcoSpatial discusses the FRIDAS framework, a standard for GIS data quality in Biodiversity Net Gain. Listen now 363. David Overton: SplashMaps 9 Nov 2026 Ed and David discuss SplashMaps growth, personalized and heritage maps, and the U.S. market. Listen now 362. Ed/Steven: Geomob Barcelona summary 2 Nov 2026 Ed and Steven chat about Geomob Barcelona, AI, Geospatial Security, OpenCage & Lessons from Foursquare Listen now Popular podcast topics: Cartography Earth Observation Ed & Steven updates Geospatial Origins Open Source Geo OpenStreetMap Geo Start-ups / business See all podcast episodes Global Geomob Supporters OpenCage : an easy, open, worldwide, affordable, geocoding API",
